    <string name="lora_guide_section">HOW TO SET ONE UP</string>
    <string name="lora_guide_step1">Get a supported board: a Heltec WiFi LoRa 32 V3, a Heltec Wireless Tracker or a LILYGO T3-S3.</string>
    <string name="lora_guide_step2">On a computer, open oshi-messenger.com/lora/flash in Chrome or Edge, plug the board in by USB and flash it. It takes about a minute.</string>
    <string name="lora_guide_step3">Unplug it, switch it on and keep it near your phone.</string>
    <string name="lora_guide_step4">Tap it under Nearby nodes above. You pair it once.</string>
    <string name="lora_guide_step5">Choose the region it will be used in. Until you do, the node listens but never transmits.</string>
    <string name="lora_guide_link">Open the flasher</string>
    <string name="lora_guide_footer">Once paired, OSHI uses the node by itself: Bluetooth and Wi-Fi first for whoever is close, LoRa when nobody is. Expect a few kilometres in a city, and considerably more with height and open ground.</string>

    <string name="lora_pairing_section">PAIRING</string>
    <string name="lora_pairing_picker">How it pairs</string>
    <string name="lora_pairing_pin">Code on the node</string>
    <string name="lora_pairing_pin_detail">Ask for a 6-digit code shown on the node\'s screen. Safer, and what the node does out of the box.</string>
    <string name="lora_pairing_nopin">No code</string>
    <string name="lora_pairing_nopin_detail">Pairs on a single tap. Choose this if your node has no screen.</string>
    <string name="lora_pairing_footer">Only affects how this phone connects to the node over Bluetooth. It changes nothing about how your messages are encrypted.</string>

